            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0438" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/195: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-02"
                            >June 2, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received June 2—12:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2424. Exchange negotiations—Japan. Department’s 1392 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1329</hi>], May 23. Swiss Legation Tokio telegraphed May 31 following:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Japanese Government sees no objection to separate British and American
                            exchanges so that American exchange can take place about July 10 as
                            agreed.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
